{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.obstruction_residual_gap","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.obstruction_residual_gap","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qou_obstruction_reduction"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.core_with_gap_gives_conclusions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.core_with_gap_gives_conclusions","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/obstruction_residual_gap.lean#L144-L154","doc":"**What closing C11 requires, stated as a theorem rather than a hope.** Supply\nthe single equation `κ₀ = χ(A)` and every conditional conclusion of\n`thm:qou-obstruction-reduction` follows for a structural core — conclusion\n(a) from the literature inputs, (c) from the equation plus the definitional\nvanishing predicate. Nothing else in the context is load-bearing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.structuralCore_not_force_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.structuralCore_not_force_gap","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/obstruction_residual_gap.lean#L132-L142","doc":"**The structural inputs do NOT force `κ₀ = χ(A)`** — the context docstring's\nclaim that the trace gap \"is NOT derivable from the two structural inputs\",\nnow proved rather than asserted. `gapWitness` satisfies Van den Bergh duality\nand Drinfeld rigidity while `κ₀ ≠ χ(A)`.\n\nCombined with `structuralCore_hhCohDim_two` this separates the block's\nconclusions exactly: (a) follows from the literature inputs; (b) and (c) are\nindependent of them and rest solely on the trace computation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.gapWitness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.gapWitness","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/obstruction_residual_gap.lean#L122-L130","doc":"An explicit structural core with `χ(A) = 0` but `κ₀ = 1`. Both literature\ninputs hold; the two integers differ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.structuralCore_hhCohDim_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.structuralCore_hhCohDim_two","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/obstruction_residual_gap.lean#L117-L120","doc":"**Conclusion (a) IS reached by the structural inputs alone**: CY-3 duality\ncomposed with Drinfeld rigidity gives `dim HH² = 1`, with no trace data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.StructuralCore.drinfeld_rigidity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.StructuralCore.drinfeld_rigidity","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/obstruction_residual_gap.lean#L115-L115","doc":"Drinfeld rigidity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.StructuralCore.vdb_duality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.StructuralCore.vdb_duality","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/obstruction_residual_gap.lean#L113-L113","doc":"Van den Bergh / Calabi–Yau duality in dimension 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.StructuralCore.kappa0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.StructuralCore.kappa0","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/obstruction_residual_gap.lean#L111-L111","doc":"The primitive Kummer obstruction integer `κ₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.StructuralCore.chi_A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.StructuralCore.chi_A","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/obstruction_residual_gap.lean#L109-L109","doc":"Euler characteristic `χ(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.StructuralCore.hhHomDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.StructuralCore.hhHomDim","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/obstruction_residual_gap.lean#L107-L107","doc":"`dim_k HH_i(U_q, Ad)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.StructuralCore.hhCohDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.StructuralCore.hhCohDim","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/obstruction_residual_gap.lean#L105-L105","doc":"`dim_k HH^i(U_q, Ad)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.StructuralCore.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.StructuralCore.mk","kind":"ctor","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/obstruction_residual_gap.lean#L103-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.StructuralCore","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.StructuralCore","kind":"structure","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/obstruction_residual_gap.lean#L100-L115","doc":"The context's **structural core**: the two literature inputs\n(`vdb_duality`, `drinfeld_rigidity`) together with the raw dimension data and\nthe two integers, but *without* any trace field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.context_residual_is_kappa_eq_chi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.context_residual_is_kappa_eq_chi","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/obstruction_residual_gap.lean#L87-L93","doc":"**The residual, at the class.** For any context, the gap discharged by\n`obstruction_trace_gap` is equivalent to the single equation `κ₀ = χ(A)` —\nwhich the context grants. Recording it in this form makes the audit target\nunambiguous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.chern_character_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.chern_character_iff","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/obstruction_residual_gap.lean#L80-L85","doc":"The same for the Chern-character field: given the cast, `φ₁ = trace χ(A)` is\nexactly `φ₁ = (χ(A) : ℝ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.residual_gap_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap.residual_gap_iff","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/obstruction_residual_gap.lean#L63-L78","doc":"**The trace-pairing apparatus is decorative.** Given that the pairing is the\ncanonical cast (`trace_pairing_cast`), the Hattori–Stallings hypothesis\n`trace_pairing χ(A) = κ₀` says *precisely* `κ₀ = χ(A)` and nothing more.\n\nStated over free data rather than over the class, so that it characterises\nthe *shape* of the hypothesis rather than merely re-deriving what an instance\nalready grants. ","signatureChunk":0}]}